# Copy to omarchy.conf to override defaults. Environment variables win over
# this file, and this file wins over the built-in defaults.

# --- Omarchy release -------------------------------------------------------

# Pinned so a silent upstream bump cannot change what you install.
# Run './omarchy-vm iso --latest' to see whether a newer release exists.
# OMARCHY_VERSION="3.8.4"

# Upstream publishes no checksum for the ISO. The first download records the
# SHA-256 it received in a .sha256 sidecar and re-checks it on later runs. Set
# this to a digest you trust to get real verification instead.
# OMARCHY_ISO_SHA256=""

# --- VM resources ----------------------------------------------------------

# Defaults are tuned for a 14-core (10P/4E), 24 GB M4 Pro. Under TCG, more
# vCPUs than you have performance cores costs more than it returns.
# VM_CPUS="6"
# VM_MEMORY="8192"          # MB
# VM_DISK_SIZE="120G"       # sparse qcow2, only grows as the guest fills it

# 'max' advertises everything TCG can emulate, which is the most compatible
# option. Narrow it only if you hit an illegal-instruction crash.
# VM_CPU_MODEL="max"

# Emulated audio costs CPU you may prefer to spend elsewhere. Set to 0 to drop
# the sound device entirely.
# VM_AUDIO="1"

# --- Networking ------------------------------------------------------------

# Host port forwarded to the guest's SSH. Change it if 2222 is taken.
# SSH_PORT="2222"

# VNC display number for headless mode; the port is 5900 plus this.
# VNC_DISPLAY="1"

# The account you created during the Omarchy install, so './omarchy-vm ssh'
# needs no argument.
# OMARCHY_USER=""

# --- Storage ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the ISO, disk image and runtime sockets live. Point this at an external
# volume if your internal disk is tight.
# OMARCHY_MAC_STATE="$HOME/.local/share/omarchy-mac"
